{
  "_comment": [
    "SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for the translation clusters. Read by BOTH",
    "src/config/i18n.ts (which builds the hreflang sets and the page routes) and",
    "astro.config.mjs (which builds the sitemap's alternate links and the",
    "content-freshness map). It is JSON rather than TypeScript because",
    "astro.config.mjs is plain ESM and cannot resolve the '@/' TypeScript path",
    "aliases — so the config used to keep its own hand-copied duplicate of this",
    "list. That duplicate silently went stale the moment a locale was added, and",
    "a stale copy here means the sitemap advertises a translation cluster that",
    "the pages themselves do not declare: exactly the partial, non-reciprocal",
    "hreflang that makes Google discard the whole cluster. One file, both",
    "readers, no drift.",
    "",
    "'locales' is ordered; 'en' must be first because it is the x-default.",
    "Every group must carry a route for every locale — i18n.ts is typed to fail",
    "the build if one is missing."
  ],
